Build Sony's NW-A57 3.10.26 tree with today's tools and without Sony's Android build around it.

- arch/arm: `.section ..., #alloc, #execinstr` -> "ax" (and #alloc,#write -> "aw", #alloc -> "a").
  Binutils 2.42 no longer reads the old flag syntax (upstream Linux made the same change).
- drivers/misc/mediatek/Makefile: drop `obj-y += imgsensor/src` and `flashlight/src`. With no
  trailing slash Sony's make never linked them; linking them now defines every kd_sensorlist
  symbol twice (the player's kernel uses BBDMP5_linux/imgsensor's copy).
- arch/arm/mach-mt8590/BBDMP5_linux/common/: the partition headers Sony's build generates and the
  source release left out. Every value is read back from the shipped kernel's own PartInfo_Private
  (40 rows) and MBR_EBR_px (10 rows); pmt.h is the platform's common copy. MBR_COUNT is 10 here.

build.sh also passes what Sony's ProjectConfig supplied: MTK_TB_WIFI_3G_MODE=WIFI_ONLY (otherwise
mtk_ccci_helper.c calls modem power functions this SoC build does not have) and two include paths
(ion.h, lcm_drv_mt8127.h).

